okay so I want to talk a little bit  today about Republican congressman Dan  Crenshaw he was on the Joe Rogan program  not that long ago and he said a bunch of  stuff that really didn't make sense  about socialism and healthcare and Joe  Rogan pretty effortlessly sort of made  mincemeat of Dan Crenshaw's arguments  and I did a story about it and there was  great interest in it and clearly some of  my audience has been following Dan  Crenshaw since because I got a bunch of  emails this morning about an interview  that Dan Crenshaw gave to Fox &amp; Friends  I believe it was yesterday and I want to  go through some of the things in this  interview because it actually seems dan  Crenshaw is a dangerous guy in a very  particular way he seems not just  uninformed but actually delusional and  he presents his delusional uninformed  ideas in an eloquent and sort of Ben  Shapiro type way where it's like wow he  seems so convinced that this is so  obviously the truth that it clearly must  be even when what he's saying doesn't  really make any sense and as a result  he's become a real conservative hero to  a lot of right-wingers who were just  looking to have red meat thrown at them  and talking points that they can use so  this is it it's scary to see that he's  almost becoming like a pseudo  intellectual figure among some on the  right and I know you'll be scared by  that idea but I wanted to get into a  just a couple of the things he said  yesterday during this Fox and Friends  interview so first of all here he is  railing against Marxism which he says  there's been a concerted effort to bring  to the United States for decades take a  listen to this always part of the plan  it has been for decades actually and and  it started well back into until window  and Marxism made its way into the United  States in the 60s and they're always  looking to to take advantage of some  kind of situation to make people think  that their country is evil so that they  can justify their own Marxist revolution  that is what's happening here and you  can't be blind to that the plan for  decades for Marxism to come to the  United States  in order to make people believe the  United States is evil in order to cause  a Marxist revolution so what he's taking  here is like maybe a 1% accurate idea  that in Marxism there is this idea that  when capitalism fails there will be a  revolution which will usher in a marxist  state that that that's a Marxist idea  that's true but you've really got to  break down what he's saying piece by  piece because it's a Gish gallop it's  just gift gallop is a debate term where  you just throw out a bunch of stuff and  particularly on Fox News Brian Kilmeade  is not going to be the guy to go through  step-by-step so first he says there's  been a plan for decades whose plan a  plan by whom where was it crafted  because the Marxists themselves are  almost completely non-existent like  there's not even that many socialists  most socialists are not actually  Marxists either Marxism has been around  as a theory since the 1800s so who  exactly has been working on this plan  for decades to bring this 1800s idea to  the United States for decades and if  they've been doing it for decades  they've clearly failed miserably because  there are still almost no Marxists at  all in the United States and certainly  no Marxists in positions of power so so  that part is not true then he sort of  starts taking advantage of this idea of  the left wants to make the u.s. look bad  or portray the US as evil and this is  maybe easier to do right now because the  left is in the opposition when you have  Donald Trump this wild authoritarian  surrounded by right-wing nuts in power  we are rightly pointing out that a lot  is going wrong in the country but that  doesn't mean we're Marxists or  socialists I'm certainly neither and  he's taking advantage of the situation  that has left the  left that has placed the left in a  position of having to say the u.s. is a  bad actor in some cases the US is a bad  actor on coronavirus because of the  failed response from Trump and mostly  Republican governors that doesn't mean  the country is in and of itself bad  that's a very simplistic and childish  sort of way to categorize countries it's  cartoonish thinking the real view is the  United States as a country given how  rich we are could be a force for so much  more good than it is and that's what we  want to get back to and it doesn't mean  a socialist takeover or a Marxist  uprising  so again gish gallop from Dan Crenshaw  here's another clip where Crenshaw  blames the police brutality the  anti-police brutality protesters for the  spike in cases in Texas rather than  Texas reopening too early let's take a  look at that but we're gonna get through  this it's a virus without a vaccine and  we always knew this kind of thing would  happen especially when we had tens of  thousands of people in the streets just  a couple weeks ago okay this shouldn't  have just sort of surprised no one over  300 cities 300 plus cities had some type  of rioting looting protests happening  how do people not link those two in fact  I've seen reports saying no proof that  the riots in the streets in the protests  led to the rise of coronavirus you'd  have to suspend logic to think that yeah  don't believe your lying eyes everybody  wants to say it was a few people hanging  out of bars that caused this that's not  true listen Texas has been reopening  since May first okay we've been getting  back to normalcy since May first and  everything was declining as a result  cases were declining this spikes  happened after tens of thousands of  people got together in close proximity  I again there's nothing wrong with  saying that that's that's just the truth  and we're just dealing with it now it's  not about blaming anybody it's just  about being honest with with causes and  effects so notice that Brian Kilmeade  says you know we had rioting and looting  and protesting like what we mostly had  was actually protesting this is a  linguistic tool that's used you first  mentioned the rioting and the looting  and then you mentioned the protesting  always frame things as mostly violent  when you're against the mess  but the real meat here is the cases  which Dan Crenshaw says is him being  honest listen we got to be honest it's  the anti-police brutality protests that  spiked cases now I set up front the  virus knows no political ideology the  virus doesn't care whether you're  protesting against lockdowns or you're  protesting against police brutality both  can spike cases the facts happen to be  that the anti lockdown protests were  mostly people not wearing masks whereas  the anti-police brutality protests were  mostly people wearing masks not  everybody you saw a few masks at the  anti lockdown protests and you saw a few  people without masks at the anti-police  brutality protests but by and large  people were wearing masks and the masks  work even sean hannity set it on his  program last night so in New York City  and in Boston we had huge protests and  we didn't have a spike and in fact we  see a continued decline in New York and  Massachusetts in other places you had  protests and there has been a spike and  the spike appears to be mostly because  of people without masks and restaurants  we're hearing about outbreaks at nail  salons and the like and even Texas his  own governor said we probably opened  bars too early which is certainly an  admission that things have not gone  exactly right so I have my ideology as  truth and my ideology is health I was  worried there would be a major spike  because of the protests  fortunately the protesters widely wore  masks and it doesn't seem as though  those protests caused a big spike  conversely we're starting to see some  elements surrounding Tulsa Oklahoma that  are seeing more rapidly increasing cases  that could be because of Trump's rally  at which 6,200 people crowded together  well crowded there was there was some  room because it was so empty but many of  them were crowded together without  wearing masks let's just tell the truth  and don't fall for Dan Crenshaw's BS

